# Online multiplayer backend configuration.
#
# The client app never talks to Firebase directly. Instead it calls the
# same-origin /api/* serverless functions (see the /api folder), which proxy
# to Cloud Firestore from Vercel's servers. This keeps online play working
# from networks where Google's API endpoints are unreachable (e.g. Iran).
#
# Only the two variables below are needed; they are read by the serverless
# functions at runtime (they are no longer used by the client bundle).
#
# Where to find these values:
#   Firebase console (https://console.firebase.google.com)
#   -> your project -> Project settings (gear icon) -> General
#   -> Your apps -> Web app -> SDK setup and configuration -> Config
#
# Local development: copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
#   cp .env.example .env
# (.env is git-ignored; never commit real keys.)
#
# Vercel: add the same variables in
#   Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables
#   then trigger a Redeploy so the functions pick them up.

REACT_APP_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
REACT_APP_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional aliases the /api functions also accept (without the REACT_APP_
# prefix):
# FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
